  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "num": "01",
      "en": "{Imagine} a child standing on a {diving} board {four feet} high and asking himself the question:“Should I jump?”This is what {motivation} or the lack of it can do.Motivation and goal setting are the two {sides} of the same {coin} .Without motivation, you can {neither} set a goal nor {reach} it.Like the child on the diving board, you will stay {undecided} .",
      "cn": "<u> 想象 </u> 一下，一个孩子站在 <u> 四英尺 </u> 高的 <u> 跳 </u> 板上，问自己这个问题：“我应该跳吗？”这是 <u> 动力 </u> 或缺乏动力带来的情形。动力和目标设定是同一枚 <u> 硬币 </u> 的正反两 <u> 面 </u> 。没有动力，你 <u> 既不 </u> 能设定目标，也无法 <u> 实现 </u> 目标。就像跳板上的这个孩子一样，你会 <u> 犹豫不决 </u> 。"
    },
    {
      "num": "02",
      "en": "So how should you motivate yourself? How should you stay motivated to {achieve} the goal? First, you need to {evaluate} yourself-your values, your {strengths} , your weaknesses, your achievements, your {desires} , etc.Only then should you realize your goals.Just as a {camel} {endures} the harsh conditions of the desert, people have their {respective} abilities to help them persevere ( (坚持) ).",
      "cn": "那么，你应该如何激励自己呢？你应该如何保持动力来 <u> 实现 </u> 目标呢？首先，你需要 <u> 评估 </u> 自己，包括你的价值观、 <u> 优势 </u> 、劣势、成就、 <u> 愿望 </u> 等。只有这样，你才能实现你的目标。就像 <u> 骆驼 </u> 能够 <u> 忍受 </u> 沙漠的恶劣环境一样，每个人都有 <u> 各自的 </u> 能力来帮助自己坚持下去。"
    },
    {
      "num": "03",
      "en": "You also need to judge the {quality} and {depth} of your motivation.This is {quite} important, because it is {directly} related to your {commitment} .There are times when your heart is not in your work.This can {affect} your work.So, {slow} down and think about what you really want to do at that {moment} .Clarity of {thoughts} can help you move {forward} .",
      "cn": "你还需要判断动力的 <u> 质量 </u> 和 <u> 深度 </u> 。这一点 <u> 非常 </u> 重要，因为它与你的 <u> 投入直接 </u> 相关。有时候你的心思不在工作上，这就会 <u> 影响 </u> 你的工作。所以， <u> 慢 </u> 下来，想想你那个 <u> 时刻 </u> 真正想做什么。清晰的 <u> 思路 </u> 可以帮助你 <u> 向前 </u> 迈进。"
    },
    {
      "num": "04",
      "en": "{Another} way of setting {realistic} goals is to {analyze} your {short} and long-term {objectives} , keeping in mind your beliefs, values and strengths.Even running race {winners} need to run {lap} after lap to build endurance ( (耐久力) ).Instead of trying to lose thirty {kilos} in a month, aim to lose a kilo per week.Don't aim to climb over a {fence} that's too high without preparation.Remember that goals are {flexible} .They can change {according to circumstances} .They also need to be {measurable} .",
      "cn": "设定 <u> 现实的 </u> 目标， <u> 另一种 </u> 方法是 <u> 分析短期 </u> 和长期 <u> 目标 </u> ，同时记住你的信念、价值观和优势。即使是跑步比赛的 <u> 获胜者 </u> 也需要 <u> 一圈 </u> 又一圈地跑，以此建立起耐力。与其试图在一个月内减掉30 <u> 公斤 </u> ，不如设定每周减掉一公斤的目标。不要在没有准备的情况下就试图翻越太高的 <u> 栅栏 </u> 。记住，目标是 <u> 灵活的 </u> ，它们可以 <u> 根据情况 </u> 而改变，还应是 <u> 可衡量的 </u> 。"
    },
    {
      "num": "05",
      "en": "Your personal circumstances are {equally} important.For example, you may want to be a pilot but can't become one because your {eyesight} is not good enough.However, this should not {discourage} you.You should {reassess} your goals, and motivate yourself to set a new goal.",
      "cn": "你的个人情况 <u> 同样 </u> 重要。例如，你可能想成为一名飞行员，但却不能实现，因为你的 <u> 视力 </u> 不够好。不过，这不应 <u> 让 </u> 你 <u> 气馁 </u> 。你应该 <u> 重新评估 </u> 你的目标，并激励自己设定一个新的目标。"
    },
    {
      "num": "06",
      "en": "You will surely need to {overcome} some difficulties, some planned, but most unplanned.You will easily throw in the {towel} without {ample} motivation.Make sure that you plan for these difficulties.Don't turn a {deaf} {ear} to advice.By working with someone else, you can {double} your efforts and {sail} more smoothly towards your goals.",
      "cn": "你肯定需要 <u> 克服 </u> 一些困难，一些是计划中的，但大多数是计划外的。如果没有 <u> 足够的 </u> 动力，你会很容易 <u> 放弃 </u> 。所以应确保做好应对这些困难的计划。不要对建议充 <u> 耳不闻 </u> 。通过与他人合作，你可以使努力 <u> 加倍 </u> ，更顺利地 <u> 驶向 </u> 你的目标。 MKqjwFu4arM4cgPc+LiB66EBg/AaE0u6XBr6IpfU5EiRRdX6Ad+uTD+Kdly4W5UG"
    }
  ],
